menu "libpd"

config LIBPD_FLOAT_DSP
    bool "Use single-precision DSP optimisations"
    default y
    help
        Optimise the Pd 0.56-5 maths, oscillator, table lookup and vline DSP
        routines for processors without hardware double precision. Scheduling
        timestamps remain double precision. Disable for stock Pd routines.

config LIBPD_IRAM_DSP
    bool "Place common Pd DSP routines in IRAM"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    default n
    help
        Place current arithmetic, buffers, envelopes, filters, oscillators,
        interpolated table and delay reads, maths and DSP dispatch routines
        in internal instruction RAM. Includes scalar and unrolled variants.
        Consumes internal SRAM otherwise available for data and heap.
        This improves instruction placement, not full cache-disabled safety:
        called helpers and signal/table data can remain in flash or PSRAM.
        Disable to restore normal flash placement without changing DSP code.

endmenu
